egal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"A creature blocked by a creature enchanted with Cracked Skull still needs to assign damage equal to the enchanted creature's toughness (minus any damage already marked on the enchanted creature) before trampling over to a player, planeswalker, or battle.","oracle_id":"4415b65d-5473-4b19-94f7-e5cf4ce64d5e","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Sporogenic Infection's second ability can target any player, not just the controller of the enchanted creature.","oracle_id":"659a259d-f75e-4af3-b568-c63225e647de","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A token copy of Sprouting Phytohydra is created even if the damage dealt to Sprouting Phytohydra destroys it.","oracle_id":"66847507-f8bb-4266-bd6e-a91c0baf0000","published_at":"2006-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Cytoshape turns a creature into a copy of Sprouting Phytohydra, and that creature is dealt damage, the token that is put onto the battlefield is simply a copy of Sprouting Phytohydra. At the end of the turn, the Cytoshaped creature will revert back to what it was, but the token copying it will not.","oracle_id":"66847507-f8bb-4266-bd6e-a91c0baf0000","published_at":"2006-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token copy of Sprouting Phytohydra is dealt damage, it will create another token copy.","oracle_id":"66847507-f8bb-4266-bd6e-a91c0baf0000","published_at":"2006-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature with trample blocked by a creature enchanted with Cryoshatter still needs to assign damage equal to the enchanted creature’s toughness (minus any damage already marked on the enchanted creature) before trampling over to a player, planeswalker, or battle.","oracle_id":"865715e9-6759-4e01-803d-702c959e386e","published_at":"2025-07-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cryoshatter may target and may enchant a creature that’s already tapped. An ability that triggers when a creature “becomes tapped” won’t trigger until the creature changes from being untapped to being tapped.","oracle_id":"865715e9-6759-4e01-803d-702c959e386e","published_at":"2025-07-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the enchanted creature is tapped as a cost to activate a mana ability, the mana ability resolves immediately, then Cryoshatter’s last ability goes on the stack.","oracle_id":"865715e9-6759-4e01-803d-702c959e386e","published_at":"2025-07-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the enchanted creature is tapped as a cost to cast a spell or to activate an ability that’s not a mana ability, Cryoshatter’s last ability will go on the stack on top of that spell or activated ability. Cryoshatter’s last ability resolves first (destroying that creature), then the spell or activated ability resolves.","oracle_id":"865715e9-6759-4e01-803d-702c959e386e","published_at":"2025-07-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When the enchanted creature becomes tapped or is dealt damage, Cryoshatter’s last ability triggers. That creature will be destroyed when the ability resolves, even if Cryoshatter has left the battlefield or is somehow enchanting a different creature by then.","oracle_id":"865715e9-6759-4e01-803d-702c959e386e","published_at":"2025-07-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can choose to put zero tokens or all the tokens onto the battlefield. You can't choose a number in between.","oracle_id":"b0a54050-3493-4ff6-8eca-e43b92c1f3d3","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Mire Blight’s ability triggers, the creature it was enchanting at that time is the one that will be destroyed when the ability resolves. It doesn’t matter if Mire Blight leaves the battlefield or somehow becomes attached to another creature by that time.","oracle_id":"fcfbe3b8-a955-45d8-9329-3af565a3b53c","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Mire Blight’s ability triggers when the enchanted creature is dealt any kind of damage, not just combat damage.","oracle_id":"fcfbe3b8-a955-45d8-9329-3af565a3b53c","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
